# The vault is its own git repository, and ClaudeGitPushAll commits and pushes
# it every night. Two things that live here must never be part of that commit:
#
#   daily/.pending/   raw session tails dropped by the session-* hooks, waiting
#                     for a flush that has not run yet. They are UNPROCESSED
#                     transcript text — the input to the pipeline, not its
#                     output — so pushing them publishes verbatim session
#                     content (and, on a repo with a remote, publishes it
#                     off-box) hours before anything decided what belongs in the
#                     wiki at all.
#   .processed.json   the pipeline's state ledger, plus its lock and temp files.
#                     Machine-local bookkeeping: committing it means every clone
#                     of the vault claims to have already processed transcripts
#                     it has never seen, and two machines fight over the file on
#                     every pull.
#
# The .gitkeep exception keeps the empty directory in the tree, which is what
# makes the skeleton deployable.
daily/.pending/*
!daily/.pending/.gitkeep
.processed.json
.processed.json.*
